cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "The Generational Lineage Engine"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/michaelrendier/GenerationalLineage"
authors:
  - family-names: Allison
    given-names: Cody Michael
    alias: Michael Rendier
    email: the.wandering.god@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7239-6760"
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit for exact factoral decomposition of numbers, operators, words, sequences,
  permutations, processes, units and groups, on two lines: descent (free) and ascent (paid, or
  refused with a statement of what is owed). Twenty-eight toolsets share one contract and check
  themselves; every tutorial transcript is generated by running the code.
keywords:
  - factorization
  - decomposition
  - number theory
  - cryptanalysis
  - string periodicity
  - Lyndon words
  - Berlekamp-Massey
  - Mellin transform
